<item>
            <title>[LU-20937] sanity test_154ea: cleanup removes unrelated test directories</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20937</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_154ea fails because its EXIT cleanup attempts to remove unrelated test directories. The readdir assertion itself did not fail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In change 69468 patchset 3, enforced RHEL 8.10 ldiskfs DNE testing reported:&lt;br/&gt;
rm: cannot remove &apos;/mnt/lustre/d125.sanity&apos;: Input/output error&lt;br/&gt;
rm: cannot remove &apos;/mnt/lustre/d22.sanity&apos;: Input/output error&lt;br/&gt;
test_154ea returned 1&lt;br/&gt;
FAIL 154ea (51s)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/469f4a87-437f-47fb-add3-876720c62d7f&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/469f4a87-437f-47fb-add3-876720c62d7f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test set: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c0e8f6e0-4382-4d3e-9421-1419b06c9178&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c0e8f6e0-4382-4d3e-9421-1419b06c9178&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The pre-existing test in lustre/tests/sanity.sh registers:&lt;br/&gt;
stack_trap &quot;rm -rf $MOUNT/&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;abcdeg&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;*&quot; EXIT&lt;br/&gt;
This includes every d*.sanity directory, rather than only the long filenames created by this test. The subshell cleanup returns nonzero and the test framework reports test_154ea returned 1.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same cleanup defect predates this patch. On unrelated change 64875/16, ldiskfs DNE testing on 2026-07-15 reported:&lt;br/&gt;
rm: cannot remove &apos;/mnt/lustre/d60g.sanity&apos;: Directory not empty&lt;br/&gt;
test_154ea returned 1&lt;br/&gt;
FAIL 154ea (57s)&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7c51fabb-e1dd-4738-8517-cfbf99a21a81&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7c51fabb-e1dd-4738-8517-cfbf99a21a81&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Change 64875/17 also had the same cleanup failure on ZFS:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/16cd22aa-e1ab-4ac8-8062-ebf294f60825&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/16cd22aa-e1ab-4ac8-8062-ebf294f60825&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The broad cleanup has been present since commit 609fc54142 (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18138&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_154e: @@@@@@ FAIL: .lustre returned by readdir &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18138&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18138&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, 2024-08-13), which is on the target branch. Change 69468 only reserves an unused connection flag, adds its display name, and wire checks. It changes neither this test nor directory removal behavior. There are no unmerged parents in this checkout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow found no linked tickets or candidates. JIRA searches for 154ea, the affected directory names, and cleanup glob behavior found no covering ticket. &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18138&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_154e: @@@@@@ FAIL: .lustre returned by readdir &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18138&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18138&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; concerns .lustre being returned by readdir; &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-7344&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_154g test30 fail on cleanup: FAIL: test_154g failed with 1&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-7344&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-7344&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; concerns connection loss during test_154g, neither describes this cleanup defect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Restrict cleanup to the files created by test_154ea. The underlying I/O errors on unrelated directories are not diagnosed by this report. No guest reproduction was needed for the cleanup defect, which is explicit in the code and both sets of logs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69468-ps3-2f2d8eb9b0c5 on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/69468&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69468&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
